How about the following ideas to dampen the poly-pile glut:
  - polymorphing a wand will never create a polymorph wand.
  - Any magic item with charges (or +n bonus points) will never exceed
       a +1 or +3 or so; likewise wands never have more than 3 charges.
  - The sum of all such bonus points in the poly-pile will not exceed
       n times the charges left in the polymorph wand (n >= 1).

Oh, yes: a previous post mentioned (among lots of other things)
a Water Level.  I have no knowledge of the source, so I don't know
what would be involved to add a boat (or raft etc) to the game for
use on the water.
   I think that a lake about half the screen's size would be a neat
and formidable thing to encounter!  I don't know about sunken
treasures, but maybe a Wand of Probing would reveal what's sunk,
and zapping a Wand of Levitation into the water would raise the stuff
to the surface ...

